<title>INDIA: India money market inactive as Bombay banks closed.</title>
<headline>India money market inactive as Bombay banks closed.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's money market was closed as banks in Bombay, the main commercial centre, were closed for a Moslem holiday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The overnight call money rates closed at 0.10-0.4 percent on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India holds an auction of 30 billion rupees of ten-year securities on April 21.</p>
